--TEST--
two `for` headers declaring the same counter is `rule:types/declaration`'s re-declaration diagnostic, not a new rule — `rule:iteration/for-counter-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:iteration/for-counter-scope` buys no new scoping: the counter is function-scoped, so a
// second header declaring the same name is the answer `rule:types/declaration` already
// gives for any re-declared name, naming the first declaration.
for (int $i = 0; $i < 2; $i = $i + 1) {
    echo $i;
}
for (int $i = 0; $i < 2; $i = $i + 1) {
    echo $i;
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0406]: `$i` is already declared
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
